{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head da44a00bc4a9e018ac44c128bf402025550dbfd1 (tree 31aba139715bc4dd86d736b1d3e0e8bf9a1a2ebe), CJ-1 on published 15fe9f3e: the option-position `--json` scan, the typed outcome and the JSON envelope for `remote`, `show` and `acts`, with the repaired generated Page module. The verdict binds the CJ-1 implementation promise 380ed640 and signs all 18 path artifacts, with packages/cli/src/line.ts first.\n\n## Evidence\n- **Artifacts.** The 18 filed artifacts equal the 18 changed paths (`git diff --no-renames --name-only 15fe9f3e da44a00b`): none missing, none extra, none twice. No path sits under `examples/`, so no signed release packet changes.\n- **Gate.** `gate.txt` (SHA-256 `c3c6306d…`) names head 97fa302e and tree 62554279, shows \"changed files 0\", ends \"gate passed\", and `gate.exit` reads 0 (1,643.10 s). Plain 5,126 with one skipped, Native 1,256 with two skipped, Node 246, Counting 60, crossings 0 lost, 5 stale, 0 unowned. Scale tests ran because `command-repository.ts` moved. END act cc4dec7e matches. The review head differs from 97fa302e only in the implementation note (`git diff --name-only 97fa302e da44a00b`), so no second gate applies.\n- **Failed gate.** END be79997a records the earlier gate at 8347f1fa (exit 1, 44.39 s), where workspace pins stopped on the committed Page module. The note keeps it as its own record, and the repair commit c316ea1a regenerates the module. The failure is not relabelled.\n- **Hashes.** All 31 distinct SHA-256 values in the note match: 23 against files in the retained evidence directories, and the other 8 against the committed generated module and the Page and OAuth HTML and script values. The module at 15fe9f3e hashes to `e0de86ac…` (2,509,201 bytes) and at da44a00b to `7bb232eb…` (2,516,263 bytes), as the note and the failed END state. The six HTML and script hashes appear in the retained `before.log`, `after-1.log` and `after-2.log`.\n- **Checks.** The merge into origin/main (15fe9f3e) is clean with tree 31aba139. `git diff --check` is clean. `check-commit-messages` flags none of 6. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings. The added lines carry no other project's name and no `/Users/` path. The only `generalbusiness` hits are the public `@generalbusiness/dap-*` import scope.\n\n## Wake rate\nNo alarm, retry or reschedule is added, and no server request changes. The head adds a client-side command output mode and a regenerated static page module. The wake floor and requests per room per hour are unchanged.\n\n## Architecture\n- **One carrier.** A command builds a typed result or a typed error (`Typed` on `Outcome`). The text renderer prints `lines`, which stay the private carrier of the existing words. The JSON renderer (`envelope`) takes only the typed value and never reads `lines`, an exception, a path or argv. `command` in `line.ts` drops `typed`, so the text path is unchanged.\n- **One scan.** `scanJson` mirrors `parse`: a value-taking option consumes its next token, even `--json`, which then stays data. `mcp` has its own four value options. The table in `json-output.test.ts` covers `--`, unknown options, `dev --port --json`, `scope-index inventory --out --json` and the `mcp` cases.\n- **Closed commands.** `JSON_COMMANDS` holds `remote`, `show` and `acts`. `NO_JSON_OUTPUT` lists every other finite command, and the test checks that it is exactly the commands without a renderer. `mcp` and `dev` (`long-lived`) and `scope-index` (`operator-command`) keep their own codes.\n- **Read mode.** `run(…, \"read\")` reports a lost reply as `unreadable` with `dispatch: \"none\"`. The default mode stays `mutation` (`unknown`, `dispatch: \"possible\"`), so an unconverted command cannot claim a read-only lost reply.\n\n## Security\n- **Transient carrier and private process boundary.** `mainJson` writes one compact document and one newline to standard output and returns the document's exit. The process test (`json-process.test.ts`) spawns the launcher with `mcp --json` and checks exit 2, empty standard error, one line and `exit` equal to the process status.\n- **Typed error provenance.** Every error comes from a closed factory with a fixed template. `{reason}` takes only a kebab-case native reason (`nativeReason`, up to 64 characters) and otherwise reads `unknown`. No template takes a path, key name, argv, exception text or child output. `ConfigDirectoryError` now carries a code, so a config failure names no path. `read` carries the native refused Read unchanged, as revision 6 of the design says. `JSON.stringify` escapes control characters, and the test \"remote keeps raw JSON values while escaping member text output\" pins both renderers.\n- **Adversarial no-side-effect dispatch.** `mainJson` ends with usage/2 for `mcp`, `dev`, `scope-index` and every `NO_JSON_OUTPUT` command before `configDir()`, any file, any port and any request. The scan runs before the early `dev`, `check` and `new` dispatch in `main`. The test \"JSON mcp, dev and scope-index are usage/2 before the config directory is selected, and no request is sent\" covers it. An unexpected exception ends as the fixed `unexpected-error`.\n- **Browser claim and invitation dependency boundary.** The Page and OAuth bundles carry claim and invitation helpers through `command-support.ts` into `json-output.ts`. The retained `closure.log` lists nine CLI inputs (browser-helpers, browser, claim, command-support, invitations, json-output, read-session-cache, shown-text, store-signer) and none of `main.ts`, `line.ts` or `config-dir.ts`. `nodeBuiltinMarkerAfter` reads false for both scripts, and the committed module holds no `node:fs`, `node:path`, `node:os` or `node:child_process`. The fixed read-session refusal template is present in both rebuilt scripts (`closedTemplateAfter` true, `closedTemplateBefore` false).\n- **Generated output.** The Page HTML (`62339a1e…`) and OAuth HTML (`87e3ea59…`) are unchanged. Page JS moves from `e76cd829…` to `d8406c0d…` and OAuth JS from `c1404ad8…` to `e89becaf…`. Two builds on the matching lock view gave identical bytes (`after-1.log`, `after-2.log`).\n- **Seals.** `security-entry-points.test.mjs` changes the seals of exactly the changed owners (`command-targets`, `command-scope`, `command-repository`, `command-support`, `line`). The Node stage passed with them at the gated tree.\n- **Consumed credential and live act path.** The note keeps the clone path validation and the live act dispatch unchanged, and the focused tests it cites passed.\n\n## Simplification\nThe envelope, the scan and the typed carrier add one module and one table, and every later slice removes commands from `NO_JSON_OUTPUT`. I see nothing to remove.\n\n## Non-blocking\n1. **Design table wording.** The CJ-1 row in `notes/2026-10-12-cli-json-output-design.md` reads \"CJ-1 envelope (implemented in candidate)\". After landing, \"in candidate\" reads stale. Change it to \"built\" at the next edit.\n2. **Undocumented flag.** `--json` appears in neither `USAGE` nor a user document. `dap remote --json` works today. Add the usage line and a short how-to when CJ-2 lands.\n3. **Page bundle size.** The CLI error templates (`MESSAGES` in `json-output.ts`) now ship in both scripts, about 3.7 KB and 3.0 KB, because `command-support.ts` imports them. A later slice can split the templates the browser never uses.\n4. **Deployment.** The room Worker serves the regenerated page module, so a deployment that includes this head changes the Page and OAuth scripts. No schema or table changes, so rollback is safe. Read the DO rate after that deploy.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:cef8c8fd92c524c058c51bbbce903915bc3fdb8b","binding":"assigned","head":"da44a00bc4a9e018ac44c128bf402025550dbfd1","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d2c9063e0a5285379300833a29d88290ed298758\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:90d9da40258799b9b1006f75ef17a